  "note": "First election after the wartime postponement: the whole council of fifteen, polled Wednesday 18 September 1946 and counted on Thursday in the Town Hall by Geo. McGowan, town clerk and returning officer. Eighteen candidates. Asterisk = outgoing member. Labels as printed: U. Unionist, I. Independent, C.W.L. Commonwealth Labour; \"all ten of the Unionist candidates were returned\" (Belfast News-Letter). The News-Letter prints Irwin 1,309 (Portadown News 1,305) and the fuller names J. S. Davison, T. W. T. Jackson, Mrs Ethel Walker and W. A. Camblin, which are used here. Mrs Walker, Davison and Irwin were described in 1947 as unofficial Unionists."
}
